   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public authorities law, in relation to confidentiality agreements",
    "basePrintNo": "S5915",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5915-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §2853, Pub Auth L",
    "lawSection": "Public Authorities Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5915\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act to amend the public authorities law, in relation to\nconfidentiality agreements\n\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF THE BILL :\nTo ban the use of employee confidentiality agreements for public\nauthorities, except where information is protected by FOIL.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\nAdds new section 2852 to the Public Authorities Law. Bars the use of\nconfidentiality agreements between state and local authorities and\ntheir employees. Exceptions are made for information that is already\nprotected by current state law. In the event there is a conflict over\nwhether information is protected or not this bill directs authorities\nto establish a process for determining this.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nNew York's public Authorities have a long history of operating without\nproper public scrutiny.  The state has acted in recent years to reform\nthese entities.  This bill continues that trend and protects employees\nof public authorities.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nA.11506 (2007-2008).\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
